Infected port: scene counters and options (vglSceneOptions, vglSceneHint).
Counts scenes begun (display / framebuffer object), the time spent beginning them, the scissor mask-update draws (at a scene's begin and at a scissor change), depth surfaces made and depth loads spared; all in vglGetStats. vglSceneHint(1) tells vitaGL the next framebuffer scene starts with a full depth clear; with vglSceneOptions(depth_trim) a build that force-loads the depth (STORE_DEPTH_STENCIL) then skips the load. The release build never loads depth, so there it only counts. vglSceneOptions(.., mask_skip) is an experiment, off by default: it leaves out the full-target mask-update draw at the start of a scene without a scissor.

